# Cloudflare Pages response headers for the app.
#
# Vite copies everything in app/public/ into app/dist/, which is what
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml uploads, so this file lands in the build output
# root where Pages parses it. It is not served as an asset itself.
#
# It exists because the cutover of 3 September 2026 would otherwise have dropped a
# policy the old shell had: tools/build_site.py wrote nosniff, the referrer policy
# and the cache rules into site/_headers on every deploy, and site/ retires with
# that shell. This file is the replacement, and it is the ONLY place the app's
# headers are stated.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# One immutable artifact per deploy, so the shell must never be cached hard: a
# reader holding a stale index would silently be reading an older board with no
# way to know.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# DELIBERATELY NOT `immutable`, and this differs from what build_site.py wrote.
# That file's /data/* rule carried its own condition -- "content-addressed by the
# deploy itself ... once the split lands". The split has now landed and the data
# files are NOT content-addressed: app/src/data.ts fetches `data/<name>.json` at a
# fixed path with no hash and no query. A year of `immutable` on those paths would
# leave a returning reader on the new shell reading last month's research, which is
# precisely the failure this repo keeps writing down. Revalidate instead; the files
# are small and the responses are 304s.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# These ARE content-addressed: Vite writes a hash into every filename it emits, so
# a changed file is a changed URL and the old one can be held forever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
